#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:12
msgid "Introduction to RST and Sphinx for Textbook Contributors"
msgstr "Introducción a RST y Sphinx para colaboradores de libros de texto"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:19
msgid "What is RST?"
msgstr "¿Qué es la RST?"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:21
msgid ""
"RST stands for ReStructured Text. It is the standard markup language used "
"for documenting python packages. Sphinx_ is the Python package that "
"generates an html website from RST files, and it is what we are using to "
"generate this site. To read more about why we chose RST over markdown or "
"Latex, read the following section, :ref:`heading_why_rst`."
msgstr ""
"RST significa ReStructured Text. Es el lenguaje de marcado estándar "
"utilizado para documentar paquetes en python. Sphinx_ es el paquete de "
"Python que genera un sitio web html a partir de archivos RST, y es el que "
"estamos utilizando para generar este sitio. Para leer más sobre por qué "
"elegimos RST en lugar de markdown o Latex, lee la siguiente sección, "
":ref:`heading_why_rst`."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:27
msgid "Why RST?"
msgstr "¿Por qué RST?"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:28
msgid ""
"Out of the box, RST supports globally-defined styles, figure numbering and "
"referencing, Latex function rendering, image display customization and more."
" Furthermore, restructured text was already the language of choice for the "
"AguaClara ecosystem's documentation."
msgstr ""
"De serie, RST soporta estilos definidos globalmente, numeración y "
"referencias de figuras, renderizado de funciones Latex, personalización de "
"visualización de imágenes y más. Además, el texto reestructurado ya era el "
"idioma preferido para la documentación del ecosistema AguaClara."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:35
msgid "Setting up RST for Development"
msgstr "Configuración de RST para el desarrollo"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:36
msgid ""
"There are two ways to *quickly* view an RST file. The first is using an "
"Atom_ plugin that renders the view alongside the source code. This is a good"
" initial test to make sure the RST is proper RST and looks *mostly* correct."
" However, some functionality, such as any extensions provided by Sphinx_ "
"won't run in the preview. In order to see the final html that will display "
"on the website, you'll need to use the second method, running sphinx locally"
" to fully generate the html code. Once you are satisfied with your work and "
"want to push it to the textbook, you'll need to incorporate it to the master"
" branch. To do so, refer to `Publishing online`_."
msgstr ""
"Hay dos formas de visualizar *rápidamente* un archivo RST. La primera es "
"usar un plugin Atom_ que renderiza la vista junto con el código fuente. Esta"
" es una buena prueba inicial para asegurarse de que la RST es la RST "
"correcta y se ve *en su mayoría* correcta. Sin embargo, algunas "
"funcionalidades, como cualquier extensión proporcionada por Sphinx_, no se "
"ejecutarán en la vista previa. Para ver el HTML final que se mostrará en la "
"web, tendrás que usar el segundo método, ejecutar Sphinx localmente para "
"generar completamente el código html. Una vez que estés satisfecho con tu "
"trabajo y quieras enviarlo al libro de texto, tendrás que incorporarlo a la "
"rama maestra. Para ello, consulta `Publishing online`_."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:42
msgid "Installing the Atom Plugins"
msgstr "Instalación de los plugins de Atom"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:43
msgid ""
"If you are using the Atom IDE to write RST, you can use the `rst-preview-"
"pandoc <https://atom.io/packages/rst-preview-pandoc>`_ plugin to auto-"
"generate a live RST preview within atom (much like the markdown-preview-plus"
" preview page.) To get rst-preview working, you'll need to install "
"`language-restructuredtext <https://atom.io/packages/language-"
"restructuredtext>`_ via atom and Pandoc_ via your command line (``$pip "
"install pandoc``). If everything worked, you can use ``ctrl + shift + e`` to"
" toggle a display window for the live-updated RST preview."
msgstr ""
"If you are using the Atom IDE to write RST, you can use the `rst-preview-"
"pandoc <https://atom.io/packages/rst-preview-pandoc>`_ plugin to auto-"
"generate a live RST preview within atom (much like the markdown-preview-plus"
" preview page.) To get rst-preview working, you'll need to install "
"`language-restructuredtext <https://atom.io/packages/language-"
"restructuredtext>`_ via atom and Pandoc_ via your command line (``$pip "
"install pandoc``). If everything worked, you can use ``ctrl + shift + e`` to"
" toggle a display window for the live-updated RST preview."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:49
msgid "Building RST Locally with Sphinx_"
msgstr "Construir RST localmente con Sphinx_"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:50
msgid ""
"We use Sphinx_ to build RST locally and remotely. Follow these steps to get "
"Sphinx_ and run it locally:"
msgstr ""
"Usamos Sphinx_ para construir RST local y remotamente. Sigue estos pasos "
"para obtener Sphinx_ y ejecutarlo localmente:"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:52
msgid ""
"Get `Python 3.5+ <https://www.python.org/downloads/>`_ and pipenv "
"(:code:`$pip install pipenv`)"
msgstr ""
"Consigue `Python 3.5+ <https://www.python.org/downloads/>`_ y pipenv "
"(:code:`$pip install pipenv`)"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:53
msgid ""
"Install all dependencies and setup a virtual environment with :code:`$pipenv"
" install`"
msgstr ""
"Instala todas las dependencias y configura un entorno virtual con "
":code:`$pipenv install`"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:54
msgid ""
"Whenever you want to issue commands, start your virtual environment with "
":code:`$pipenv shell` - exit it with :code:`$exit`"
msgstr ""
"Siempre que quieras emitir comandos, inicia tu entorno virtual con "
":code:`$pipenv shell` - sálvalo con :code:`$exit`"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:55
msgid ""
"Generate all the html by navigating in the command line to the source "
"directory /Textbook and creating the build in that directory with the "
"command line :code:`$make html`."
msgstr ""
"Genera todo el HTML navegando en la línea de comandos hasta el directorio de"
" origen /Textbook y creando la compilación en ese directorio con la línea de"
" comandos :code:`$make html`."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:56
msgid ""
"View the html generated in the /Textbook/_build directory by copying the "
"full file path of /Textbook/_build/html/index.html and pasting it into your "
"browser."
msgstr ""
"Consulta el HTML generado en el directorio /Textbook/_build copiando la ruta"
" completa del archivo /Textbook/_build/html/index.html y pegándolo en tu "
"navegador."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:58
msgid ""
"Regarding **1.** the master branch for the package implementing disqus in "
"sphinx `is broken <https://github.com/Robpol86/sphinxcontrib-"
"disqus/pull/7>`_, which is why we use a non-standard pip/online "
"installation. If you already have the incorrect sphinx-disqus version "
"installed, uninstall it with ``pip uninstall sphinxcontrib-disqus`` before "
"installing the functioning version."
msgstr ""
"Respecto a **1.** la rama maestra del paquete que implementa disqus en "
"Sphinx `está rota <https://github.com/Robpol86/sphinxcontrib-"
"disqus/pull/7>`_, por eso usamos una instalación no estándar de pip/online. "
"Si ya tienes instalada la versión incorrecta de Sphinx-Disqus, desinstálala "
"con ``pip uninstall sphinxcontrib-disqus`` antes de instalar la versión "
"funcional."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:63
msgid "Building PDF Locally"
msgstr "Generación local de PDF"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:64
msgid ""
"To check errors with the PDF generation more quickly, it may be worthwhile "
"to setup your local machine to build the PDF."
msgstr ""
"Para comprobar los errores en la generación del PDF más rápido, puede valer "
"la pena configurar tu máquina local para crear el PDF."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:66
msgid "install `MikTeX <https://miktex.org/howto/install-miktex>`_"
msgstr "instalar `MikTeX <https://miktex.org/howto/install-miktex>`_"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:67
msgid "install `Perl <https://strawberryperl.com/>`_"
msgstr "instalar `Perl <https://strawberryperl.com/>`_"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:68
msgid "run the command make latexpdf"
msgstr "ejecuta el comando make latexpdf"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:69
msgid "the PDF will be created in the latex folder inside the _build folder"
msgstr "El PDF se creará en la carpeta Latex dentro de la carpeta _build"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:76
msgid "Publishing Online"
msgstr "Publicación en línea"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:77
msgid ""
"GitHub Actions builds every pull request with Sphinx and automatically "
"publishes the textbook after changes are merged into ``master``."
msgstr ""
"GitHub Actions compila cada pull request con Sphinx y publica "
"automáticamente el libro de texto una vez que los cambios se fusionan en "
"``master``."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:79
msgid ""
"Test your build by first :ref:`building RST locally "
"<heading_building_rst_locally>`."
msgstr ""
"Prueba tu build por primera :ref:`building RST locally "
"<heading_building_rst_locally>`."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:80
msgid ""
"Submit a `pull request to master <https://github.com/AguaClara-"
"Reach/Textbook/pulls>`_ and request a reviewer. Every pull request **must** "
"be reviewed by at least one other person."
msgstr ""
"Envía una solicitud pull `a Master <https://github.com/AguaClara-"
"Reach/Textbook/pulls>`_ y solicita un revisor. Cada pull request **debe** "
"ser revisada por al menos otra persona."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:81
msgid ""
"Wait for the **Test** workflow to complete successfully in the pull "
"request's checks."
msgstr ""
"Espera a que el flujo de trabajo **Test** se complete correctamente en las "
"comprobaciones de la solicitud de tirada."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:82
msgid ""
"After approval, merge the pull request into ``master``. The "
"**Documentation** workflow will build and publish the updated textbook "
"automatically."
msgstr ""
"Tras la aprobación, fusiona la solicitud de pull en ``master``. El flujo de "
"trabajo **Documentación** construirá y publicará automáticamente el libro de"
" texto actualizado."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:84
msgid ""
"If the update is not published, check the `Documentation workflow "
"<https://github.com/AguaClara-Reach/Textbook/actions/workflows/build-"
"docs.yml>`_ in GitHub Actions."
msgstr ""
"Si la actualización no se publica, consulta el flujo de trabajo de "
"`Documentación <https://github.com/AguaClara-"
"Reach/Textbook/actions/workflows/build-docs.yml>`_ en Acciones de GitHub."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:90
msgid "Testing Online"
msgstr "Pruebas en línea"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:91
msgid ""
"Open a pull request to run the same Sphinx HTML build used by the publishing"
" workflow. The pull request's **Test** check reports whether the textbook "
"builds successfully. For visual review, build the textbook locally and open "
"``Textbook/_build/html/index.html`` in a browser."
msgstr ""
"Abre una solicitud pull para ejecutar la misma compilación HTML de Sphinx "
"que usa el flujo de trabajo de publicación. La comprobación **Test** de la "
"solicitud pull informa si el libro de texto se compila correctamente. Para "
"una revisión visual, compila el libro localmente y ábrelo "
"``Textbook/_build/html/index.html`` en un navegador."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:97
msgid "Brief Best Practices"
msgstr "Breves mejores prácticas"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:98
msgid ""
"When writing RST, there are often many ways to write the same thing. Almost "
"always, the way with the fewest number of characters is the best way. "
"Ideally, never copy and paste."
msgstr ""
"Al escribir RST, a menudo hay muchas formas de escribir lo mismo. Casi "
"siempre, la forma con el menor número de caracteres es la mejor. Idealmente,"
" nunca copiar y pegar."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:104
msgid "How do I write RST?"
msgstr "¿Cómo escribo RST?"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:106
msgid ""
"RST is friendly to learn and powerful. There are many useful cheatsheets, "
"like `this one <https://thomas-"
"cokelaer.info/tutorials/sphinx/rest_syntax.html#inserting-code-and-literal-"
"blocks>`_. When you start writing RST, look at the cheat sheets all the "
"time. Use :code:`ctrl-f` all the time to find whatever you need."
msgstr ""
"RST es fácil de aprender y potente. Hay muchas hojas de trucos útiles, como "
"`esta <https://thomas-cokelaer.info/tutorials/sphinx/rest_syntax.html"
"#inserting-code-and-literal-blocks>`_. Cuando empieces a escribir RST, mira "
"las hojas de trucos todo el tiempo. Úsala :code:`ctrl-f` todo el tiempo para"
" encontrar lo que necesites."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:108
msgid "**Things not covered in most cheat sheets which are of critical importance:**"
msgstr ""
"**Cosas que no se cubren en la mayoría de las hojas de trucos y que son de "
"importancia crítica:**"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:110
msgid ""
"A document is referred to by its title, as defined between the ``*****`` "
"signs at the top of the page, **NOT** the filename. So it is critical to "
"have a title."
msgstr ""
"Un documento se denomina por su título, definido entre los signos de "
"``*****`` en la parte superior de la página, **NO** el nombre del archivo. "
"Por eso es fundamental tener un título."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:111
msgid "Anything else you'd like to add for the future..."
msgstr "¿Algo más que quieras añadir para el futuro..."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:117
msgid "Example to Start From"
msgstr "Ejemplo para empezar"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:118
msgid ""
"This file is written in RST. You can start there! Just click on \"View page "
"source\" at the top of the page."
msgstr ""
"Este archivo está escrito en RST. ¡Puedes empezar por ahí! Solo tienes que "
"hacer clic en \"Ver fuente de la página\" en la parte superior de la página."

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:126
msgid "Converting Markdown to RST"
msgstr "Conversión de Markdown a RST"

#: ../../Textbook_Creation_Help/rst_intro.rst:127
msgid ""
"Ideally, use pandoc to do the conversion in the command line: :code:`pandoc "
"--from=markdown --to=rst --output=my_file.rst my_file.md`. Raw html will not"
" be converted (because it is not actually markdown), and tables are "
"converted poorly. You'll need to carefully review any page converted with "
"pandoc."
msgstr ""
"Idealmente, usa pandoc para hacer la conversión en línea de comandos: "
":code:`pandoc --from=markdown --to=rst --output=my_file.rst my_file.md`. El "
"HTML en bruto no se convertirá (porque en realidad no es markdown), y las "
"tablas se convierten mal. Tendrás que revisar cuidadosamente cualquier "
"página convertida con pandoc."

